            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Prince Philip</strong><br>\nPrince Philip was born on the island of Corfu in Greece on June 10, 1921. His family was exiled from Greece when he was just an infant after a military coup. Philip's early life was marked by upheaval and he moved through various European countries, being educated in France, Germany, and the United Kingdom. Despite his royal lineage, his family was not wealthy, and he relied on relatives and scholarships for his education.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Naval Career</strong><br>\nPhilip joined the British Royal Navy in 1939 at the age of 18, during World War II. He served with distinction in the Mediterranean and Pacific Fleets. After the war, he continued his naval career, rising to the rank of commander before retiring from active service. His time in the navy was a significant period of his life, providing him with a sense of purpose and duty.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Marriage to Queen Elizabeth II</strong><br>\nPhilip married then-Princess Elizabeth in 1947, after a short engagement. Their marriage was a significant event in Britain, providing a sense of hope and renewal after the war. Philip gave up his Greek and Danish royal titles to become a British subject and was made the Duke of Edinburgh on the eve of the wedding by King George VI.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
