          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Retirement from Public Duties</strong><br>\nIn 2017, Prince Philip retired from public duties after decades of service. By then, he had completed over 22,000 solo engagements and given nearly 5,500 speeches. His retirement marked the end of an era for the British Royal Family, as he had been a constant presence at the Queen's side.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Legacy</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Prince Philip was occasionally seen at public events but largely stayed out of the spotlight. He passed away on April 9, 2021, at the age of 99. His legacy is multifaceted, with contributions to public life, the environment, and the monarchy, remembered by many for his service and dedication.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Mourning</strong><br>\nPrince Philip's death was mourned across the UK and the world. His passing was marked by tributes from leaders, charities, and individuals who had been influenced by his work. His funeral was held at St. George's Chapel, reflecting his wishes for a minimal fuss and honoring his military affiliations and contributions to public life.</p>\n"
              },
